    NO INVARIANCE OF THE ACTION RELATES eta TO gamma.
    (a) FDiff: E_i is a covector for any eta, the gradient operators are
        scalars for any gamma -- each term is separately invariant, so the
        variation is eta*0 + gamma*0.  (b) no shift symmetry (W(u) != 0).
    (c) Weyl: all three derivative operators share weight 2w, the clock
        term w+2, so no w is Weyl flat and the ratio gamma/eta is Weyl
        invariant anyway.  (d) conservation is the Noether identity
        Pdot.EOM = 0: it holds for every (eta,gamma).

