    so at p >> p_* the scalar's speed IS gamma/eta.

The leading interaction is the cubic term of W:
    W = u^2/(2K) + u^3/(3Ka0) + u^4/(4Ka0^2)+... ,  u = K|P|,
    so L3 = -(K^2/(3 a0)) |grad sigma|^3  and, canonically (sigma_c = sqrt(Z) sigma),
    L3 = -(K^2/(3 a0 Z^{3/2})) p^3 sigma_c^3 .
    One-loop 2-point: deltaPi/omega^2 = K^4/(144 pi^2 a0^2 Z^3 kappa_L^6 p^2),
    kappa_L = sqrt(alpha/B).  Setting = 1 gives the strong-coupling momentum.
    kappa_L = sqrt(alpha/B) = 1.186794e+24 eV^-1  (the Lifshitz mass M_L = 1/kappa_L = 8.426063e-25 eV)

    IR branch (Z ~ B):  p_sc = K^2/(8.485 pi a0 alpha^{3/2}) = 2.8360e-69 eV
